# config/defconfigs/experimental.config — Edge/QEMU base + Phase-B experiment flags ON
#
# Target: same as `qemu`/`edge` (RISC-V 64 / QEMU virt / Edge profile) but with
#         the in-flight Phase-B innovation experiments enabled BY DEFAULT.
#
# This is the honest way to ship "experiments on by default": the base Kconfig
# keeps `default n` for each flag (so a plain build never silently claims an
# unimplemented feature), and THIS profile opts both in. Build with:
#     make defconfig-experimental && make
#
# Flags enabled here (vs Kconfig defaults):
#   CONFIG_MULTISTREAM_SCHED_PRIORITY=y — RFC-0028 / I2. Control stream preempts
#       bulk on the multi-stream link.
#       STATUS 2026-08-28: RFC-0028 is **rejected** (KILL1). The re-measured
#       hold-off ratio is 8.4-8.6x over 14 paired boots, not the >= 10x target,
#       and 8.0x is the arithmetic ceiling at 16 KiB / 1460 B chunks (the 3 B
#       multi-stream header spills each chunk across the 1460 B MSS). The
#       earlier "~10x, measured" claim was a single n=1 pairing and does not
#       reproduce - see the Results section of rfcs/RFC-0028.
#       The production chunked-interleave sender (Phase D) was never built, so
#       this flag still selects a FIFO-equivalent seam. Kept as a config seam
#       only; do NOT read it as an accepted optimisation.
#   CONFIG_CONTROL_PLANE_ASYNC=y — RFC-0030 / I-12. Stackless cooperative async
#       control plane (~8.8x cheaper task resume, measured proxy).
#       NOTE: the async executor is not yet built; until it lands this flag is
#       inert at runtime (seam + measurement only).
#
# Neither is `accepted`: RFC-0028 is `rejected` (seam kept, see above) and
# RFC-0030 is `experiment-running`. Promote to the base defaults
# only when their mechanisms are implemented + validated end-to-end.
#
# Everything else inherits Edge/QEMU Kconfig defaults via `olddefconfig`.
#
# Regenerate with:  make defconfig-experimental && make savedefconfig
#
# CONFIG_DOMAIN_ROBOT=y (wave 11): MULTISTREAM_SCHED_PRIORITY lives in the
# Robot menu, which is shown only for the Robot domain; olddefconfig drops a
# value set on a hidden option, so without this line the flag would be lost.

CONFIG_DOMAIN_ROBOT=y
CONFIG_MULTISTREAM_SCHED_PRIORITY=y
CONFIG_CONTROL_PLANE_ASYNC=y
# CONTROL_TXN_TICKS is now ACCEPTED (default y in Kconfig) — no longer listed here.
